relais.description:
Currently: {url}

Alarm lamp (switch "Weckerlampe"): one minute before the alarm the red lamp is on and the main light goes to 3 % rising to 10 %. While ringing red blinks, the lamp double-flashes, the beacon is on, main light 100 %. Snooze: all off, main light 10 %. After dismissing: beacon 5 s, red fast 5 min, lamp blinks 5 min, main light 50 % for 10 min, then off within 30 s, then the beacon for 10 s more.

The main light must be dimmable and only joins within the time window; empty = no main light.

saeule.description:
Currently: {url}

Mode "Auto": the status drives the tower, every change is announced and then holds. "Manual": the lamps are switched one by one.

The flashing beacon has its own switch and applies in both modes. In status Alarm it turns itself on once red and the hint lamp start alternating - not during the announcement - and goes back to its previous state when the alarm ends.
